1
00:00:00,007 --> 00:00:01,925
3RD FLOOR GIANT LABYRINTH

2
00:00:02,009 --> 00:00:03,343
BANQUET

3
00:00:03,427 --> 00:00:04,428
HAUNTED HOUSE

4
00:00:04,511 --> 00:00:05,929
TAKOYAKI

5
00:00:10,017 --> 00:00:10,976
EIMEI FESTIVAL

6
00:00:11,059 --> 00:00:12,436
[boy 1] Don't hit anything.

7
00:00:13,437 --> 00:00:15,063
[boy 2] To the right. The right.

8
00:00:15,147 --> 00:00:16,148
[boy 3] Let's lift it.

9
00:00:16,231 --> 00:00:17,441
[boys] One, two, three...

10
00:00:20,527 --> 00:00:22,946
SNOW WHITE SCRIPT

11
00:00:31,288 --> 00:00:32,956
[all exclaiming]

12
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:34,332
Looks like it's ready.

13
00:00:36,877 --> 00:00:38,879
[opening theme song playing]

14
00:01:03,195 --> 00:01:06,656
BLUE BOX

15
00:02:11,179 --> 00:02:13,431
You can't tell me that
the day before the festival!

16
00:02:13,515 --> 00:02:15,225
{\an8}Oh, come on, Inomata.

17
00:02:15,308 --> 00:02:16,685
{\an8}EPISODE 19
I'VE GOT PLANS

18
00:02:16,768 --> 00:02:20,730
{\an8}This just means that your play is gonna
have to start about ten minutes earlier.

19
00:02:21,273 --> 00:02:23,900
A little mistake slipped through
on the pamphlet, so...

20
00:02:25,152 --> 00:02:28,113
Year one, Class B, 3:30 start.

21
00:02:28,196 --> 00:02:29,447
There we go.

22
00:02:29,531 --> 00:02:31,449
[grunts angrily]

23
00:02:32,242 --> 00:02:33,577
[Taiki] I'll be on my way.

24
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:34,953
TEACHERS' LOUNGE

25
00:02:35,036 --> 00:02:37,831
I can't believe
he didn't check it more carefully.

26
00:02:37,914 --> 00:02:39,291
That's ten whole minutes!

27
00:02:40,041 --> 00:02:41,209
[pleasant music playing]

28
00:02:44,379 --> 00:02:48,341
<i>The hustle and bustle really makes it feel
like the day before the school festival.</i>

29
00:02:51,845 --> 00:02:52,846
[gasps]

30
00:02:58,977 --> 00:03:01,980
You're askin' Kano?
To go around the festival with you?

31
00:03:02,063 --> 00:03:03,857
There's no way that's happening!

32
00:03:04,441 --> 00:03:06,484
Like I've got a shot with her.

33
00:03:06,568 --> 00:03:08,612
I guess she looks pretty busy, too.

34
00:03:08,695 --> 00:03:09,779
[boy 2] Exactly!

35
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:12,157
[boy 1] Gazing from afar is enough for me.

36
00:03:12,240 --> 00:03:14,618
- [Taiki sighs]
- [boy 2] I wish I could join that circle.

37
00:03:14,701 --> 00:03:15,619
[boy 1] Give it up.

38
00:03:19,497 --> 00:03:20,874
Hey, Taiki!

39
00:03:21,958 --> 00:03:24,252
Have you mentally prepared to go in there?

40
00:03:24,336 --> 00:03:27,380
- Prepared?
- You're in for a surprise when you do!

41
00:03:27,464 --> 00:03:30,383
[Taiki] Don't tell me someone
broke a set piece again.

42
00:03:30,467 --> 00:03:31,843
[Takada] No, that's not it.

43
00:03:32,969 --> 00:03:35,138
- [girls exclaiming]
- You look so freakin' cute!

44
00:03:35,222 --> 00:03:37,515
[girl 2] You look so beautiful.

45
00:03:37,599 --> 00:03:39,309
[overlapping chatter]

46
00:03:39,392 --> 00:03:40,644
[pleasant music playing]

47
00:03:41,811 --> 00:03:42,896
[exclaims softly]

48
00:03:42,979 --> 00:03:44,064
[gasps]

49
00:03:44,147 --> 00:03:45,398
[girl 3] It's totally perfect!

50
00:03:45,482 --> 00:03:47,734
You really came through
with this one, Kyo.

51
00:03:47,817 --> 00:03:49,319
Mm-hm.

52
00:03:49,402 --> 00:03:51,446
At least it got finished in time.

53
00:03:51,529 --> 00:03:53,990
Oh, and our fearless leader,
tell her what you think.

54
00:03:54,074 --> 00:03:55,700
[gasps] Oh...

55
00:03:55,784 --> 00:03:56,785
Um, I...

56
00:03:57,702 --> 00:03:59,162
Yeah, it looks okay, I guess.

57
00:03:59,246 --> 00:04:01,164
[Niina scoffs] That all you've got?

58
00:04:03,458 --> 00:04:05,919
Hey! I need your help with my hair.

59
00:04:09,130 --> 00:04:11,675
[Niina] It seemed like he was
just about to say something nice!

60
00:04:12,676 --> 00:04:14,427
- You don't have to run.
- [Hina] Uh--

61
00:04:18,056 --> 00:04:20,392
[Niina] <i>I guess she felt awkward
around him, too.</i>

62
00:04:21,768 --> 00:04:23,812
- So about the play's...
- [Niina] <i>And it's not as if</i>

63
00:04:23,895 --> 00:04:26,940
<i>- Hina isn't on Inomata's mind either.</i>
- Now it's gotta be ten minutes earlier.

64
00:04:29,442 --> 00:04:30,443
Here it is.

65
00:04:30,527 --> 00:04:31,361
ONE MORE DAY!

66
00:04:31,444 --> 00:04:34,698
[Niina] <i>Is it possible something might
happen during the festival?</i>

67
00:04:49,045 --> 00:04:50,088
CREPES
TAKOYAKI

68
00:04:50,171 --> 00:04:52,465
LABYRINTH - 2-B CAFE
HISTORICAL PLAY

69
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,990
[Yukiko] What? You're kidding me, right?

70
00:05:17,907 --> 00:05:19,492
Today's the festival, isn't it?

71
00:05:20,243 --> 00:05:22,037
Why are you in workout clothes?

72
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:25,957
[Taiki] I can't go to the gym
'cause of the festival.

73
00:05:26,583 --> 00:05:28,001
So I'm going for a run.

74
00:05:28,084 --> 00:05:29,711
I'll see you a little later!

75
00:05:29,794 --> 00:05:32,464
[door opens, closes]

76
00:05:32,547 --> 00:05:35,508
[sighs] That boy
could take a day off for once.

77
00:05:36,092 --> 00:05:37,719
[footsteps running]

78
00:05:38,595 --> 00:05:40,180
[panting]

79
00:05:48,188 --> 00:05:53,109
HIT THAT SMASH!

80
00:05:59,157 --> 00:06:00,867
- Chinatsu!
- Uh.

81
00:06:01,868 --> 00:06:02,869
Taiki.

82
00:06:03,578 --> 00:06:04,996
What are you doing here?

83
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:07,624
Morning practice
because the gym is closed.

84
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,127
You know you could
take a day off for once.

85
00:06:14,464 --> 00:06:16,007
That goes for you, too.

86
00:06:17,634 --> 00:06:21,554
It's like, I have so much motivation
after the match the other day.

87
00:06:21,638 --> 00:06:22,764
I feel the same way.

88
00:06:22,847 --> 00:06:25,892
Seeing you play like that got me fired up.

89
00:06:26,601 --> 00:06:27,852
[gasps]

90
00:06:32,899 --> 00:06:36,820
Although, at this rate,
I'll never be able to catch up with you.

91
00:06:37,445 --> 00:06:40,782
Could you please take some more pit stops
on your way to greatness?

92
00:06:41,407 --> 00:06:43,535
Well, sure. I'm taking pit stops.

93
00:06:43,618 --> 00:06:44,786
That's a lie.

94
00:06:45,370 --> 00:06:48,039
Your brain is 100% basketball. [grunts]

95
00:06:49,791 --> 00:06:51,167
That's not true.

96
00:06:56,923 --> 00:06:58,341
[Taiki] <i>She's so cool.</i>

97
00:07:01,344 --> 00:07:03,555
<i>She truly lives for the sport.</i>

98
00:07:03,638 --> 00:07:04,722
You know what?

99
00:07:05,432 --> 00:07:08,643
So the band we heard the other day
is made up of second years.

100
00:07:08,726 --> 00:07:09,727
Really?

101
00:07:10,687 --> 00:07:12,730
I heard their concert is at two o'clock.

102
00:07:13,398 --> 00:07:14,899
Let's go see them together.

103
00:07:16,359 --> 00:07:17,235
[gasps softly]

104
00:07:20,530 --> 00:07:22,157
If you're not free, that's okay.

105
00:07:22,699 --> 00:07:23,992
No, I'm in!

106
00:07:24,075 --> 00:07:25,910
That's awesome!

107
00:07:25,994 --> 00:07:27,996
[alarm ringing]

108
00:07:28,079 --> 00:07:30,498
{\an8}ALARM
SNOOZE

109
00:07:30,582 --> 00:07:32,709
Oh, I've gotta get going.

110
00:07:38,006 --> 00:07:40,425
All right, so two o' clock. See you there.

111
00:07:41,176 --> 00:07:42,135
Got it.

112
00:07:44,429 --> 00:07:45,388
Got it...

113
00:07:47,015 --> 00:07:48,725
[grunts]

114
00:07:49,767 --> 00:07:50,685
[groans]

115
00:07:50,768 --> 00:07:51,895
{\an8}CONGRATULATIONS ON NATIONALS

116
00:07:51,978 --> 00:07:55,815
{\an8}[female announcer] <i>The Eimei School
Cultural Festival is now open.</i>

117
00:07:55,899 --> 00:07:57,942
{\an8}EIMEI FESTIVAL

118
00:07:58,735 --> 00:08:02,447
Here we go!
Taste my deadly Butterfly Rings! Ha!

119
00:08:05,116 --> 00:08:07,327
- [ring toss guy] Oh, what a bummer!
- [whimpers]

120
00:08:07,911 --> 00:08:09,829
- I'm going again!
- [ring toss guy whimpers]

121
00:08:09,913 --> 00:08:11,706
- She's having fun.
- [Hina squeals]

122
00:08:11,789 --> 00:08:13,958
- I wonder if she's ever nervous.
- [Hina] One more time!

123
00:08:14,042 --> 00:08:17,712
Isn't she only that upbeat
because she's probably feeling nervous?

124
00:08:20,173 --> 00:08:22,300
And the play's starting at 3:30, right?

125
00:08:23,051 --> 00:08:27,347
If she has to start getting ready by 3:00,
she's gotta pack it all in before then.

126
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:28,348
Good point.

127
00:08:29,474 --> 00:08:31,935
It's time for me
to start making my rounds now.

128
00:08:32,519 --> 00:08:34,145
What are you getting up to?

129
00:08:34,229 --> 00:08:38,107
For now, I'll go find Sho and the others,
and after that...

130
00:08:40,693 --> 00:08:43,112
All right, so two o'clock. See you there.

131
00:08:43,196 --> 00:08:44,489
Oh, you know.

132
00:08:45,323 --> 00:08:46,866
Something to do with Chinatsu?

133
00:08:48,076 --> 00:08:49,661
- See you.
- Later.

134
00:08:51,704 --> 00:08:53,873
[Taiki] <i>It's like a dream come true.</i>

135
00:08:54,624 --> 00:08:56,876
<i>Chinatsu invited me to a concert!</i>

136
00:08:59,504 --> 00:09:00,380
Huh?

137
00:09:08,012 --> 00:09:09,389
Wait, Kishi?

138
00:09:10,139 --> 00:09:11,766
Taiki Inomata!

139
00:09:11,849 --> 00:09:13,017
I've heard the stories!

140
00:09:13,101 --> 00:09:14,852
They say that you beat Yusa!

141
00:09:14,936 --> 00:09:15,895
That's your opener?

142
00:09:15,979 --> 00:09:17,939
You should take me on, too!

143
00:09:18,022 --> 00:09:20,024
But we're at a festival.

144
00:09:20,108 --> 00:09:21,150
Okay.

145
00:09:21,234 --> 00:09:23,820
{\an8}Then you gotta show me
where Chinatsu's class is.

146
00:09:23,903 --> 00:09:25,154
{\an8}I don't wanna!

147
00:09:25,238 --> 00:09:27,031
What did you just say?

148
00:09:27,115 --> 00:09:31,119
You're the one who's standing in my way
of getting her phone number, remember?

149
00:09:31,202 --> 00:09:33,454
Yeah, and it was only because you lost!

150
00:09:33,538 --> 00:09:34,664
[both grunting]

151
00:09:36,249 --> 00:09:37,667
Well!

152
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:39,669
There's a combo you don't see often.

153
00:09:41,212 --> 00:09:43,673
Hi, Haryu. And hello, Karen.

154
00:09:44,257 --> 00:09:45,341
{\an8}CULTURAL FESTIVAL ATTIRE

155
00:09:45,425 --> 00:09:46,676
MODEL GIRLFRIEND

156
00:09:47,260 --> 00:09:48,094
TWO GUYS

157
00:09:48,177 --> 00:09:49,262
SAD FIGHT

158
00:09:49,345 --> 00:09:50,179
[both grunt]

159
00:09:50,263 --> 00:09:52,599
Why are you guys having this big fight?

160
00:09:52,682 --> 00:09:54,058
Well, Miss Karen,

161
00:09:54,142 --> 00:09:57,604
this doofus won't escort me
to where Year 2 Class B is.

162
00:09:57,687 --> 00:09:58,688
"Miss Karen"?

163
00:09:58,771 --> 00:10:02,191
Well, we were just on our way there,
so why don't you tag along?

164
00:10:02,275 --> 00:10:03,568
If you don't mind!

165
00:10:03,651 --> 00:10:04,694
Although,

166
00:10:05,778 --> 00:10:08,698
it's quite stimulating, so be careful.

167
00:10:09,407 --> 00:10:10,366
[both] Huh?

168
00:10:11,784 --> 00:10:14,704
{\an8}CAFÉ

169
00:10:14,787 --> 00:10:16,372
[indistinct chatter]

170
00:10:20,793 --> 00:10:22,045
[sparkling sound]

171
00:10:22,545 --> 00:10:24,213
Hi! Welcome in!

172
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:28,968
[girl] Waitress!

173
00:10:29,719 --> 00:10:30,970
I'll be right with you.

174
00:10:31,054 --> 00:10:33,973
[both exclaiming]

175
00:10:34,557 --> 00:10:35,725
[girl] Chinatsu!

176
00:10:35,808 --> 00:10:36,976
Yes?

177
00:10:37,602 --> 00:10:39,145
Sorry for making you wait.

178
00:10:44,692 --> 00:10:45,652
[groans]

179
00:10:45,735 --> 00:10:47,236
Kishi!

180
00:10:47,820 --> 00:10:50,782
[gasping] How are you
still on your feet, bro?

181
00:10:52,075 --> 00:10:53,368
It's not easy.

182
00:10:53,451 --> 00:10:55,495
I'm fighting for my life here.

183
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:58,039
[both] She's just too cute.

184
00:10:59,832 --> 00:11:01,376
Those two are funny ones.

185
00:11:01,459 --> 00:11:02,502
They're young.

186
00:11:05,254 --> 00:11:06,839
[Taiki] <i>That was a surprise.</i>

187
00:11:06,923 --> 00:11:09,759
<i>She did tell me
she wasn't going to be a waitress.</i>

188
00:11:11,094 --> 00:11:15,515
<i>I am glad I get to see her in that outfit,
but this is just...</i>

189
00:11:16,516 --> 00:11:17,517
Hello there.

190
00:11:18,393 --> 00:11:19,560
You got a boyfriend?

191
00:11:20,103 --> 00:11:21,771
Let me have your number.

192
00:11:21,854 --> 00:11:23,022
Huh?

193
00:11:23,106 --> 00:11:24,023
[exclaims]

194
00:11:25,358 --> 00:11:28,778
We are not that kind of establishment.

195
00:11:28,861 --> 00:11:29,779
Nagisa!

196
00:11:30,947 --> 00:11:33,783
[Nagisa] So do me a favor,
and stop hitting on her.

197
00:11:34,617 --> 00:11:37,578
She and I happen to operate
on the same wavelength.

198
00:11:37,662 --> 00:11:39,414
We're a great combo.

199
00:11:39,497 --> 00:11:40,915
Like PB&J.

200
00:11:40,998 --> 00:11:44,460
Like a married couple who has
their own language to communicate.

201
00:11:44,544 --> 00:11:45,545
Nagisa...

202
00:11:46,629 --> 00:11:49,298
[Taiki] <i>Thank goodness
there's someone protecting her.</i>

203
00:11:49,382 --> 00:11:51,300
[groans]

204
00:11:51,384 --> 00:11:52,844
[Taiki] What?

205
00:11:52,927 --> 00:11:54,804
Her... boyfriend?

206
00:11:56,472 --> 00:11:58,641
Oh, no, that's one of her teammates from--

207
00:11:58,724 --> 00:12:00,935
No better cure for heartbreak
than some drinking.

208
00:12:01,018 --> 00:12:02,186
Go on, drink up.

209
00:12:02,270 --> 00:12:03,813
You're using him for profit?

210
00:12:03,896 --> 00:12:04,856
[sniffles]

211
00:12:05,398 --> 00:12:07,191
I knew it'd turn out this way!

212
00:12:07,275 --> 00:12:09,068
- [sniffles]
- [Taiki] How's he drunk?

213
00:12:09,152 --> 00:12:10,069
[Kishi cries]

214
00:12:10,153 --> 00:12:16,451
We may have had a magical meet-cute,
but it's not our destiny to be a couple.

215
00:12:17,034 --> 00:12:18,077
A magical what?

216
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:21,080
[Kishi] Look at that smile on her face.

217
00:12:23,166 --> 00:12:24,375
I'm okay,

218
00:12:24,459 --> 00:12:27,837
as long as Chinatsu lives
happily ever after, I'll be all right.

219
00:12:30,590 --> 00:12:32,717
[Haryu] That's it, drown your sorrows.

220
00:12:34,385 --> 00:12:37,763
[Taiki] <i>I want her to look happy
when it's me standing next to her.</i>

221
00:12:37,847 --> 00:12:39,849
- [footsteps approaching]
- [gasps]

222
00:12:39,932 --> 00:12:42,351
[Karen] Chii, you're doing a great job.

223
00:12:42,435 --> 00:12:44,103
[Chinatsu] You made it to the cafe!

224
00:12:44,187 --> 00:12:46,981
[Karen] I thought that outfit
might need some divine worship.

225
00:12:47,064 --> 00:12:48,107
What does that mean?

226
00:12:49,484 --> 00:12:51,277
Pardon. I'll get a refill.

227
00:12:52,361 --> 00:12:53,362
[Karen] So listen,

228
00:12:54,238 --> 00:12:57,116
{\an8}I wanna go to the fashion show.
And that starts at 2:00.

229
00:12:57,742 --> 00:12:59,118
{\an8}Chii! Let's go together.

230
00:12:59,202 --> 00:13:01,370
[Taiki] <i>What... Two o'clock is when...</i>

231
00:13:03,706 --> 00:13:05,833
Sorry, I have plans already.

232
00:13:10,796 --> 00:13:13,841
- Okay, then what about you?
- [Taiki] Ah! Would you look at the time!

233
00:13:13,925 --> 00:13:16,636
I have to go find my friends! Okay, bye!

234
00:13:17,261 --> 00:13:19,138
- What the--
- Don't leave me!

235
00:13:19,222 --> 00:13:20,973
[feel-good music playing]

236
00:13:28,606 --> 00:13:30,775
[Taiki] <i>The Cultural Festival is so fun.</i>

237
00:13:33,236 --> 00:13:35,530
MUSIC CLUB

238
00:13:35,613 --> 00:13:37,782
2:00 P.M.
SAMOYED

239
00:13:37,865 --> 00:13:40,326
SCHEDULE

240
00:13:51,295 --> 00:13:52,296
[sighs]

241
00:13:54,632 --> 00:13:57,134
<i>Chinatsu sure is running late.</i>

242
00:13:58,386 --> 00:13:59,345
[grunts]

243
00:13:59,428 --> 00:14:02,306
<i>When she said, "See you there,"
did she mean "inside?"</i>

244
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:07,853
Hey there. We are Samoyed.

245
00:14:08,396 --> 00:14:10,106
[all cheering]

246
00:14:15,403 --> 00:14:16,988
[Taiki] <i>Incredible.</i>

247
00:14:17,488 --> 00:14:18,698
<i>This is exciting.</i>

248
00:14:19,323 --> 00:14:21,158
[vocalist] Are you ready
to have a good time?

249
00:14:21,242 --> 00:14:22,326
[all cheering]

250
00:14:23,035 --> 00:14:25,246
[Taiki] <i>There are
a lot of people here, but...</i>

251
00:14:27,331 --> 00:14:30,585
<i>Wait. Maybe I misunderstood something?</i>

252
00:14:30,668 --> 00:14:31,669
SEE YOU AT TWO O'CLOCK

253
00:14:31,752 --> 00:14:33,588
<i>No, she definitely said that.</i>

254
00:14:33,671 --> 00:14:35,882
- Here's our first song.
- [Taiki] <i>Then again...</i>

255
00:14:35,965 --> 00:14:37,258
- "Nagisa."
- [all cheering]

256
00:14:37,341 --> 00:14:40,052
[Taiki] <i>If you told me
it was all just a dream,</i>

257
00:14:40,136 --> 00:14:41,846
<i>I wouldn't be surprised.</i>

258
00:14:44,265 --> 00:14:45,433
[boy] Yeah, let's go!

259
00:14:47,435 --> 00:14:49,645
[Chinatsu panting]

260
00:14:50,938 --> 00:14:52,356
I'm sorry...

261
00:14:52,440 --> 00:14:53,983
I made you wait.

262
00:15:00,990 --> 00:15:02,116
Sorry that I'm late.

263
00:15:02,700 --> 00:15:03,659
[gasps softly]

264
00:15:04,702 --> 00:15:05,870
It's that...

265
00:15:05,953 --> 00:15:08,623
The person with the shift
after mine was late.

266
00:15:08,706 --> 00:15:09,665
It's okay.

267
00:15:10,333 --> 00:15:12,209
[vocalist] All right.
Here's our next song.

268
00:15:12,293 --> 00:15:14,003
- [all cheering]
- Let's get closer.

269
00:15:14,086 --> 00:15:15,880
[music playing]

270
00:15:15,963 --> 00:15:17,256
[audience cheering]

271
00:15:18,007 --> 00:15:19,383
[Taiki] <i>What a relief.</i>

272
00:15:21,177 --> 00:15:23,012
<i>It wasn't a dream after all.</i>

273
00:15:29,268 --> 00:15:31,520
[band singing "Nagisa" by Spitz]

274
00:15:33,981 --> 00:15:37,068
This is my first concert,
but they're pretty awesome!

275
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,699
<i>I guess it's too loud for her to hear me.</i>

276
00:15:52,917 --> 00:15:54,919
I said this is pretty awesome!

277
00:15:56,587 --> 00:15:58,881
[chuckles] Mm-hm.

278
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:05,179
[Taiki] <i>Why do I feel
like we're getting closer?</i>

279
00:16:08,933 --> 00:16:12,228
<i>I wonder if I'm overthinking all of this.</i>

280
00:16:14,105 --> 00:16:16,899
<i>I keep getting my hopes up over and over.</i>

281
00:16:46,303 --> 00:16:47,888
[all cheering]

282
00:16:48,889 --> 00:16:50,057
Thank you, everyone!

283
00:16:51,726 --> 00:16:54,729
And our next song is "Blues Drive."

284
00:16:54,812 --> 00:16:56,647
- [all cheering]
- Oh! It's this song!

285
00:16:57,148 --> 00:16:58,524
Do you like this one?

286
00:16:59,275 --> 00:17:02,486
Yeah, I do, but actually,
Karen loves this song more.

287
00:17:03,237 --> 00:17:06,032
She says she listens to it whenever
she and Haryu have a fight.

288
00:17:06,115 --> 00:17:08,284
[music starts playing]

289
00:17:11,203 --> 00:17:13,205
[band singing "Blues Drive"
by Yoshitaka Yamada]

290
00:17:13,289 --> 00:17:14,790
Um, Chinatsu.

291
00:17:14,874 --> 00:17:17,543
Why did you invite me
to come with you to the concert?

292
00:17:18,127 --> 00:17:19,170
[grunts softly]

293
00:17:20,629 --> 00:17:22,673
[Taiki] <i>Ah. She couldn't hear me.</i>

294
00:17:23,549 --> 00:17:25,134
Just ignore what I said.

295
00:17:27,344 --> 00:17:29,722
<i>She probably just had
no one else to come with</i>

296
00:17:30,347 --> 00:17:33,309
<i>because Karen was saying
she wanted to see the fashion show.</i>

297
00:17:36,479 --> 00:17:37,980
[exclaims softly]

298
00:17:42,693 --> 00:17:43,903
[Chinatsu] It's because...

299
00:17:45,279 --> 00:17:46,572
Did you say some...

300
00:17:48,157 --> 00:17:49,325
[gasps]

301
00:17:56,165 --> 00:17:57,917
Hang on, what did you just say?

302
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:58,834
Uh--

303
00:17:59,710 --> 00:18:02,338
The music is too loud. Sorry!

304
00:18:26,779 --> 00:18:29,365
<i>What was it? Now I really wanna know.</i>

305
00:18:41,335 --> 00:18:42,628
That was fun, huh?

306
00:18:42,711 --> 00:18:45,381
There's just nothing
like hearing music live.

307
00:18:45,464 --> 00:18:48,134
Hey, about what you said before...

308
00:18:49,051 --> 00:18:51,053
Your class's play starts soon.

309
00:18:51,137 --> 00:18:52,638
It's at 3:30, right?

310
00:18:53,264 --> 00:18:54,098
Yeah.

311
00:18:54,181 --> 00:18:56,142
<i>So she's just gonna pretend
she didn't hear me.</i>

312
00:18:57,017 --> 00:18:59,019
I'll get a seat right in the center.

313
00:18:59,103 --> 00:19:00,855
You do know I'm not in it.

314
00:19:03,023 --> 00:19:04,066
Even so,

315
00:19:04,150 --> 00:19:06,902
I know you put a lot of work
into making it all happen.

316
00:19:10,489 --> 00:19:11,782
FLUFFY AND CHEWY CREPES

317
00:19:11,866 --> 00:19:13,993
Well, thanks for going with me.

318
00:19:14,076 --> 00:19:15,828
- See ya.
- Okay.

319
00:19:23,419 --> 00:19:24,420
[groans]

320
00:19:25,254 --> 00:19:27,840
[Taiki] <i>The Cultural Festival is so fun!</i>

321
00:19:28,757 --> 00:19:31,552
<i>Only fun things happen when you're here!</i>

322
00:19:31,635 --> 00:19:34,180
<i>We went to a concert together,
just the two of us!</i>

323
00:19:47,651 --> 00:19:52,031
<i>If my life ever flashes before my eyes,
this'll be a day I remember.</i>

324
00:19:53,157 --> 00:19:55,367
{\an8}Taiki! Hi.

325
00:19:55,451 --> 00:19:56,285
{\an8}STAMP RALLY

326
00:19:56,368 --> 00:19:58,829
- Keep up the good work, Nishida.
- What? Hang on!

327
00:19:58,913 --> 00:20:00,289
I'm super bored!

328
00:20:00,372 --> 00:20:01,332
FORTUNE TELLER

329
00:20:01,415 --> 00:20:03,792
[Taiki] All right.
What are you doing here?

330
00:20:03,876 --> 00:20:06,795
I'm a fortune teller.
As you can see, my dear sir.

331
00:20:06,879 --> 00:20:08,047
And beyond that,

332
00:20:08,130 --> 00:20:11,717
my class is running a stamp rally,
and I'm one of the stamps you can get.

333
00:20:11,800 --> 00:20:15,179
Inside, you'll find monsters and clowns,
and if you get stamps from them,

334
00:20:15,262 --> 00:20:17,056
then, you can win a prize.

335
00:20:17,139 --> 00:20:18,098
So are you in?

336
00:20:18,182 --> 00:20:19,558
No, thanks.

337
00:20:19,642 --> 00:20:20,935
{\an8}DESTINY

338
00:20:21,018 --> 00:20:22,770
{\an8}Let me at least read your fortune.

339
00:20:23,437 --> 00:20:24,813
{\an8}Can you really do that?

340
00:20:25,689 --> 00:20:27,316
{\an8}Duh. My grandma's a psychic.

341
00:20:27,983 --> 00:20:28,859
{\an8}What?

342
00:20:29,401 --> 00:20:31,362
[Nishida grunts]

343
00:20:45,334 --> 00:20:47,002
{\an8}How ominous!

344
00:20:47,086 --> 00:20:51,840
{\an8}Soon and very soon, a terrible
and unthinkable ordeal shall betide you!

345
00:20:51,924 --> 00:20:53,050
Ordeal?

346
00:20:53,133 --> 00:20:54,802
[girl] Mr. Fortune Teller!

347
00:20:56,178 --> 00:20:59,598
I followed the advice you gave me,
and I found my wallet!

348
00:20:59,682 --> 00:21:01,475
{\an8}My ex-boyfriend texted me!

349
00:21:01,558 --> 00:21:03,602
I found my long-lost brother!

350
00:21:03,686 --> 00:21:05,104
You're an amazing fortune teller!

351
00:21:05,187 --> 00:21:07,648
- [Nishida] I see. I see.
- Thank you so much!

352
00:21:07,731 --> 00:21:09,108
[Taiki groans softly]

353
00:21:09,942 --> 00:21:11,110
[Taiki] <i>No, no, no.</i>

354
00:21:11,694 --> 00:21:14,113
<i>There's no way what he said will happen.</i>

355
00:21:14,905 --> 00:21:18,117
<i>An "unthinkable ordeal"
is too vague anyway.</i>

356
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:19,118
WAITING ROOM

357
00:21:19,201 --> 00:21:21,829
<i>He probably just said
what came to his mind, and--</i>

358
00:21:21,912 --> 00:21:23,372
- [Niina] What?
- [Taiki grunts]

359
00:21:24,498 --> 00:21:27,126
The actor playing the prince
is in the hospital?

360
00:21:28,002 --> 00:21:30,045
She went to the Ninja Warrior booth.

361
00:21:30,129 --> 00:21:33,132
She fell off after reaching the goal,
and she broke her leg.

362
00:21:34,258 --> 00:21:36,635
[girl 1] Who's going
to play the prince, then?

363
00:21:36,719 --> 00:21:38,178
[girl 2] We need someone to fill in.

364
00:21:38,262 --> 00:21:40,889
Luckily, the prince
doesn't have too many lines.

365
00:21:41,640 --> 00:21:44,893
- Anyone free?
- [boy 2] No, everyone's out having fun.

366
00:21:45,477 --> 00:21:48,731
And everyone here
is an actor or needed backstage.

367
00:21:49,606 --> 00:21:51,900
And I have to help with the lighting...

368
00:21:52,901 --> 00:21:54,653
Hm. Oh.

369
00:21:54,737 --> 00:21:55,571
[grunts softly]

370
00:21:56,071 --> 00:21:56,905
Huh?

371
00:21:56,989 --> 00:21:57,990
{\an8}EIMEI FESTIVAL

372
00:21:58,073 --> 00:21:59,033
{\an8}[Niina] Oh!

373
00:22:00,701 --> 00:22:01,785
{\an8}[Taiki] Huh?!

374
00:22:05,539 --> 00:22:07,541
[closing theme song playing]
